think Crux-first among the named siblings: the segment capstone named its ONE honest weakness explicitly -- a single lumpy object with several distance peaks over-segments, one basin per peak -- and named the remedy: h-maxima suppression, keep only significant peaks. Highest-Lindy (closes the capstone's own horizon, a textbook algorithm -- grayscale geodesic reconstruction by dilation) and a genuine crux, fully agent-doable, no gates. Chose it over the disk-element builder and the size-histogram.
think Built image/hmaxima.rye owning only the h-maxima transform: sub_clamp for the marker (distance - h), relax_dilate for one geodesic-dilation step (3x3 max capped at the mask, off-image skipped), dilate_pass for Vincent's forward+backward hybrid, hmaxima iterating to a fixpoint bounded by a loud pass ceiling. markers_hmax and segment_hmax splice the suppression into segment's own seeding and end-to-end pipelines -- compose not braid, no new flood/codec/color/labeler.
think Designed the crux fixture as a 5x5 lobe fused by a one-pixel neck to a 3x3 lobe: one 8-connected component, two unequal distance peaks. Did NOT guess the threshold -- instrumented a diagnostic loop over h on metal (measurement beats memory): raw field max_distance 9, two peaks persist through h=5, collapse to one at h=6..8, vanish at h>=9. So the shallow lobe's prominence read larger than my first estimate; used h=7, the clean middle of the one-peak band, read from the metal.
obs GREEN on metal after the h correction: the OVER-SEGMENTATION crux (segment over-cuts the one component into two basins; segment_hmax returns one whole basin, no watershed line), the h=0 IDENTITY (field unchanged byte-for-byte, markers equal to raw), the FIELD-CAP invariant (reconstruction never exceeds the mask, background stays 0), a distance.colorize QOI round-trip, an EmptySource refusal by name, determinism. Witness tools/hmaxima_witness.rish GREEN.
